Day 25: Set Apart for Love | Saturday of the Third Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Be holy, for I am holy.”
Not perfection.
Not flawlessness.
An invitation to belong.

Welcome to Day 25 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection brings you into the heart of what holiness truly means. Holiness is not about being impressive — it is about being available. It is belonging to God, letting His love shape your life, and allowing His goodness to shine through your ordinary moments.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that holiness is not reserved for saints or mystics. It is for you — in your real life, your real struggles, your real imperfections. Holiness is God’s work in you, and your willingness to say yes.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why holiness is belonging, not perfection

How God sets you apart for love, mercy, and goodness

What holiness looks like in everyday life

A prayer to be shaped by God’s heart

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, make me holy.”

